  "text_md": "### focus on youth\n\n## Preparing South African youth for a nautical career\n\n##### Article and photos by Lt Cdr Glenn von Zeil, SA Naval Reserves\n\nhe motto “Honour and Skill” of the South African Sea Cadets is proudly displayed under their badge. These words embody the core values of the Corps which are: Integrity, excellence\n\n# Tand service, which are instilled in the\n\nSea Cadets via their training and interaction with competent instructors. These three words embody the cardinal points of a Sea Cadet’s compass of life and include: Honesty, morality, loyalty, responsibility, discipline, accountability, self-respect and obedience. The Sea Cadets also teach the necessary knowledge and provides practical skills underwritten by accredited courses necessary for those who wish to follow a career at sea within the maritime industry.\n\n*ABOVE: Sea Cadets* *practicing “pulling” which* *forges teamwork.*\n\n*L EF T: Sea Cadets* *undergoing survival at sea* *training while on an annual* *year end camp at the SA* *Navy’s Seamanship School* *at SAS SIMONSBERG.*\n\n### Where and when does the training take place?\n\nThe land based training ships\n\n|The Sea Cadet in South Africa||located around the country|\n|---|---|---|\n|movement traces its origins back to||provide a safe space with|\n|the first South African Training Ship|Sea Cadets are school going|competent instructors at which|\n|(TS), located on Woodstock beach Cape|boys and girls from Grade 6|training can take place. Training|\n|Town, TS Woltemade was opened on|to Grade 12 who enjoy having|takes place on Fridays or|\n|8 June 1905. The movement spread|“serious fun” while learning|Saturdays or Sundays depending|\n|throughout South Africa and currently|leadership, self-discipline and|on the training ship involved,|\n|there are 15 training ships, nine are|maritime orientated skills as a|with leadership camps scheduled|\n|active and developing those values|voluntary extra mural activity.|during the school holidays. The|\n|and skills required to ensure that the|Any youngster irrespective|highlight of the year is the annual|\n|maritime industry is provided with|of race, gender or religion is|camp hosted by the SA Navy in|\n|recruits who have a passion for the sea.|welcome.|Simon’s Town.|\n\n### Who are the Sea Cadets?\n\n**2 0 1 5 V O L 2 2 N O 1**•**S A S O L D I E R**\n",
